# {{projectName}}

Apache Camel integration generated by [FlowCamel](https://github.com/flowcamel/flowcamel).

## Prerequisites

- Java 21+

## Run locally

```bash
chmod +x mvnw   # Unix/macOS only, first time
./mvnw spring-boot:run
```

{{#if devProfile}}
With a Spring profile (overrides in `application-{{devProfile}}.yml`):

```bash
SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE={{devProfile}} ./mvnw spring-boot:run
```
{{/if}}

On Windows:

```cmd
mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
```

The app loads routes from `src/main/resources/camel/routes.camel.yaml` (one YAML file may contain **multiple** `route` entries — one per flow designed in FlowCamel).

Routes in the same project can call each other with Camel `direct:{routeId}` when you add a **Call flow** step in the designer.

## Application properties

Connection settings and secrets are in `src/main/resources/application.yml`. Values marked as secrets in FlowCamel are exported as `${property.key}` placeholders — provide real values via environment, `.env`, or your secret store at runtime.

{{#if hasVault}}
### Secrets ({{vaultProvider}})

This project is wired for **{{vaultProvider}}** via `spring.config.import` in `application.yml`. Configure IAM / managed identity and map secret JSON keys to the property paths in `application.yml` (e.g. `sftp.password`).
{{/if}}

## Build

```bash
./mvnw clean package
java -jar target/{{artifactId}}-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar
```

## Optional infrastructure

If your flow uses Kafka or ActiveMQ, start dependencies first:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

Then run the application as above.

## Project layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `pom.xml` | Maven build (Camel {{camelVersion}}, Spring Boot 3) |
| `mvnw` / `mvnw.cmd` | Maven Wrapper (no global Maven install required) |
| `src/main/resources/camel/routes.camel.yaml` | Camel YAML DSL routes |
| `src/main/resources/application.yml` | Spring Boot / Camel configuration |
{{#each exportProfiles}}
| `src/main/resources/application-{{this}}.yml` | Profile overrides for **{{this}}** |
{{/each}}
| `docker-compose.yml` | Local Kafka / ActiveMQ (when used by the flow) |
